== Part C: cs-16 regression -- a BACKPORT's corpus/classification basis is the LOWER neighbor, never the higher one ==
Read from distribution/versions.yaml's REAL array, whatever it holds today: cutting the MIDDLE
element with a higher version already sitting above it in the array. Before the fix,
gate_one()'s old_for_corpus picked max(old_window) -- the highest version ANYWHERE in the
array, unrelated -- instead of the real, lower predecessor. (Named versions were pinned here
until 2026-08-29, when the array's real contents changed under it and the guard failed on its
own premise rather than on the bug it guards; the shape is the premise, not the numbers.)
SKIP (part C): cs-16's cut-in-the-middle shape needs at least three declared versions and distribution/versions.yaml declares ['4.0.0', '5.0.0']; there is no middle to cut, so the backport comparison-basis regression cannot be exercised against the real array today

